---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const programs = [
  {
    logo: '/images/brand/rechart-stacked.svg',
    name: 'RECHART · The Wayfinder Method',
    tag: 'A self-paced programme for when the direction isn’t obvious anymore — not when life has already fallen apart.',
    href: '/wayfinder-method/',
    cta: 'Come aboard →',
  },
];

const posts = [
  {
    title: 'What does it really mean to rechart your life?',
    excerpt: 'Reinvention isn’t actually a thing psychology recognises. What it does recognise is more interesting — and a lot kinder.',
    href: '/blog/what-rechart-really-means/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Why you’re lying when you say you don’t have time for something',
    excerpt: '(And why that’s completely fine.) A small, slightly uncomfortable NLP exercise in honesty.',
    href: '/blog/why-no-time-is-a-lie/',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  description="Art of Small Steps — a gentle, evidence-informed home for self-knowledge work, built around Sophie Kemenes. Small steps, taken on purpose."
>
  <!-- 1 OPENING QUOTE -->
  <section style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:40px 8px 56px;text-align:center">
    <p style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(24px,3.4vw,38px);line-height:1.4;margin:0;color:var(--color-text)">
      &ldquo;If you want to build a ship, don&rsquo;t drum up people to collect wood and don&rsquo;t assign them tasks and work, but rather teach them to long for the endless immensity of the sea.&rdquo;
    </p>
    <p style="font-family:var(--font-hand);font-size:19px;margin:18px 0 0;color:var(--color-accent-dark)">
      &mdash; a line often (and probably wrongly) attributed to Antoine de Saint-Exup&eacute;ry
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 ABOUT ME / HOST NOTE -->
  <section style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:10px 8px 70px;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)">
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap-reverse;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;margin-top:50px">
      <div style="flex:1 1 360px;min-width:0">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-hand);font-size:22px;margin:0 0 2px;color:var(--color-accent-dark)">A note from me</p>
        <h1 style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(34px,4vw,48px);line-height:1.1;margin:0 0 18px">Hi, I&rsquo;m Sophie.</h1>
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin:0 0 14px">
          Fifteen years ago I read a prayer that stopped me mid-scroll. Not a prayer for miracles &mdash; just for strength for the everyday. <em>Teach me the art of small steps.</em>
        </p>
        <details style="margin:0 0 20px">
          <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--color-accent-dark);list-style:none">&#9656;&nbsp;Read the whole prayer</summary>
          <blockquote style="margin:14px 0 0;padding:4px 0 4px 18px;border-left:2px solid var(--color-accent);font-style:italic;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text-muted)">
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px">Lord, teach me the art of small steps.<br />I&rsquo;m not asking for miracles or visions &mdash; just strength for the everyday.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px">Make me attentive and resourceful, so I notice the knowledge and experience that really speak to me, right when I need them.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px">Steady my choices in how I spend my time. Help me feel the difference between what matters and what doesn&rsquo;t.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px">Give me strength, self-control and a sense of proportion, so life doesn&rsquo;t just sweep me along, but I can shape each day with some wisdom.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px">Help me meet whatever&rsquo;s right in front of me as well as I can, and let me treat this present hour as the most important one there is.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px">Let me see clearly that life comes with difficulties and failures too &mdash; and that these are chances to grow and mature.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px">Make me someone capable of reaching the people who are right at the bottom.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px">Give me not what I want, but what I need.</p>
            <p style="margin:0">Teach me the art of small steps. Amen.</p>
          </blockquote>
        </details>
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin:0 0 14px">
          I liked it enough to buy the domain that same day, and then did absolutely nothing with it for more than a decade. (Some small steps take a while.) I just didn&rsquo;t have anything to put there yet &mdash; only the quiet sense that one day I would.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin:0 0 14px">
          In the meantime I built an actual life out of taking those steps: as a trainer and NLP practitioner, as a corporate security lead explaining risk for a living to people who&rsquo;d rather not think about it, and &mdash; closer to home &mdash; as someone who has rerouted her own direction more than once, usually at an unreasonable hour, usually with tea.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin:0 0 18px">
          This is the house all of that lives in now. Not one big promise. A few honest ways in, depending on where you are and how much you&rsquo;ve got in you today &mdash; whether that&rsquo;s a few committed weeks, or just the next ten minutes.
        </p>
        <a href="/about/" style="font-size:15px;color:var(--color-accent-dark);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-accent)">More about me &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <figure style="flex:0 0 180px;margin:0">
        <img src="/images/wayfinder/sophie-portrait-compass.webp" alt="Sophie, a watercolor portrait: copper curls, glasses, a soft grey scarf" style="display:block;width:180px;height:180px;object-fit:cover;object-position:50% 30%;border-radius:50%;box-shadow:0 14px 34px rgba(20,34,48,.18)" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 FIND YOUR NEXT STEP (programs + downloadables, general on purpose) -->
  <section style="background:var(--color-text);color:var(--color-bg);padding:70px 24px;width:100vw;margin-left:calc(50% - 50vw);margin-right:calc(50% - 50vw);box-sizing:border-box">
    <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center">
      <p style="font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-accent);font-weight:600;margin:0 0 10px">Where to begin</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(32px,3.6vw,48px);margin:0 0 14px">Find your next step</h2>
      <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 46px;color:#C9D4DB">
        Not everything here is a big, life-reshaping programme. Some of it is. Some of it is a single page you can read in the next ten minutes. Start wherever fits today.
      </p>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:28px">
        {programs.map((p) => (
          <div style="flex:1 1 320px;max-width:380px;background:var(--color-bg);color:var(--color-text);border-radius:8px;padding:34px 30px 30px;text-align:left">
            <img src={p.logo} alt="" style="display:block;height:38px;width:auto;margin:0 0 18px" />
            <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin:0 0 20px">{p.tag}</p>
            <a href={p.href} style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:var(--color-accent-dark);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--color-accent)">{p.cta}</a>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div style="flex:1 1 320px;max-width:380px;border:1.5px dashed #4A5560;border-radius:8px;padding:34px 30px 30px;text-align:left;display:flex;align-items:center">
          <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#9FB0BA;margin:0">More ways in are on their way &mdash; smaller, standalone pieces as well as full programmes. If you want to hear when something new lands, the easiest way is through RECHART&rsquo;s own signup for now.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 FROM THE JOURNAL -->
  <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:70px 8px 90px">
    <p style="font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-accent-dark);font-weight:600;margin:0 0 10px;text-align:center">From the journal</p>
    <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(28px,3.2vw,40px);margin:0 0 40px;text-align:center">Shorter reads, same voice</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:28px;justify-content:center">
      {posts.map((post) => (
        <a href={post.href} style="flex:1 1 340px;max-width:400px;display:block;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:8px;padding:28px 26px;background:var(--color-surface)">
          <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-weight:500;font-size:22px;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--color-text)">{post.title}</h3>
          <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin:0 0 14px">{post.excerpt}</p>
          <span style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--color-accent-dark)">Read &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p style="text-align:center;margin:36px 0 0">
      <a href="/blog/" style="font-size:15px;color:var(--color-accent-dark);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-accent)">All journal entries &rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
